  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full set at the Bottom of the Hill in San Francisco, California, on Wednesday, May 26, 2004 [1][2]. This concert is the 58th in the Internet Archive’s collection for the band, following a session recorded in Amsterdam on March 27, 2004 [2]. The 68-minute recording features 19 songs, opening with “Jaipur” and “Tallahassee” before moving into “Slow West Vultures” [1]. The set includes “Going To Cleveland,” which has 8 archived performances, and “Dance Music,” the first in the archive [1][2]. Later in the show, the band plays “Song For My Stepfather,” a rare track with 11 archived performances and the first in the archive, alongside “My Favorite Things” with 13 archived performances [1][2]. The lineup continues with “Baboon” and “Pigs That Ran Straightaway Into the Water, Triumph of,” another rare entry with 11 archived performances [1][2]. The set closes with “See America Right,” preceded by a bustout titled “(Peter’s R-Kelly Ignition ringtone),” which is the first in 25 archived shows after 810 days [1][2]. This is the only available recording of this specific date [1].",
